  "goodToKnow": "Der Weltraum is outer space; das Weltall or simply das All is the universe or space. The first German in space was Sigmund Jähn from the GDR, who flew on a Soviet mission in 1978. Alexander Gerst later became famous for his ISS missions and photos. Die Raumfahrt is space travel, and der Astronaut or Raumfahrer an astronaut. The German Aerospace Center, the DLR, is based in Cologne. It has no plural."
